# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:
- **app/layout.tsx** - Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout

### What Was Done:
1. ✅ Verified @vercel/analytics package was already installed (v1.6.1)
2. ✅ Confirmed the Analytics component was imported but not rendered
3. ✅ Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout inside the `<body>` tag after `{children}`
4. ✅ Ran `npm install` to ensure dependencies are up to date
5. ✅ Verified linter - no new errors or warnings introduced by our changes
6. ✅ Updated package-lock.json through npm install

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/react' was already imported in the layout file but wasn't being rendered. I added the `<Analytics />` component in the optimal location:
- Inside the `<body>` tag
- After the `{children}` prop
- Before the Service Worker script

This placement ensures that analytics tracking is initialized after the page content loads, following Vercel's best practices for App Router projects.

## Notes
- The project uses the App Router pattern (app directory)
- Package manager: npm (package-lock.json)
- Pre-existing linting issues in app/page.tsx and public/sw.js are unrelated to this change
- The build fails due to missing Supabase environment configuration (pre-existing issue, not related to Analytics)
- The Analytics component will only send data when deployed to Vercel with analytics enabled

## Testing
- Linting passed without introducing new errors
- Dependencies installed successfully
- Changes are minimal and follow Next.js best practices
